# A live two-way WebSocket held through the ctx: an outside caller opens a
# socket at the route; the echo nodes hold the conversation, replying to each
# message with {echo, turn}. The rig opens the socket, sends two messages, and
# asserts the echoes come back. TWO echoes read the same connection: inbound
# is broadcast to every ctx reader (no node steals messages from another), so
# every message the caller sends must come back twice, once from each echo.
# The zero-Rust socket path (a Loop over `inbound`) is the socket_loop fixture.

sock = Socket { path: "__E2E_PATH__" }
echo = LiveWsEcho
echo2 = LiveWsEcho
out = Debug
out2 = Debug

echo.path = sock.path
echo2.path = sock.path
out.data = echo.done
out2.data = echo2.done
